      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\( a \\) for which \\( g(a) = 0 \\) for the function \\( g(x) = 3x - 4 \\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Set up the equation:**\n   \\[\n   g(a) = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Substitute \\( g(x) \\) into the equation:**\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( a \\):**\n   - First, isolate the term involving \\( a \\) by adding 4 to both sides of the equation:\n     \\[\n     3a - 4 + 4 = 0 + 4\n     \\]\n     Simplifying this, we get:\n     \\[\n     3a = 4\n     \\]\n\n   - Next, solve for \\( a \\) by dividing both sides by 3:\n     \\[\n     a = \\frac{4}{3}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( a \\) that satisfies \\( g(a) = 0 \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\\).",
